## Why This Is Asked
This question assesses the ability to design robust distributed signal processing algorithms that can operate under real-world constraints such as asynchrony, packet loss, and computational limitations across edge devices.

## Key Concepts
- Distributed whitening and demixing across multiple nodes
- Gossip-based consensus for matrix fusion
- Time-varying mixing matrix tracking with adaptive algorithms
- Partial observation handling and permutation alignment
- Real-time performance evaluation using SDR/SIR metrics and latency constraints

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code sketch for a single gossip round
function gossipRound(W_local, neighbors) {
  const W_agg = average([W_local, ...neighbors.map(n => n.W_local)]);
  return normalize(W_agg);
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

This question assesses the ability to integrate simple ICA with audio-visual cues under practical latency constraints, mirroring real-world video conferencing scenarios.

## Key Concepts

- **Online ICA**: Processing two-channel audio in a streaming fashion using STFT
- **Cross-modal permutation alignment**: Using lip movement as a visual cue to resolve frequency-wise permutation ambiguity
- **Feature extraction**: Lip kinematics (lip width, height, aperture) from video; spectral envelopes from audio
- **Latency considerations**: Target end-to-end latency under 100ms for real-time performance

## Code Example

```javascript
// Lip-audio alignment score computation
function computeLipAudioScore(lipKinematics, audioEnvelope) {
  const normalizedLip = normalize(lipKinematics);
  const normalizedAudio = normalize(audioEnvelope);
  return correlation(normalizedLip, normalizedAudio);
}

// Permutation resolution using visual cues
function resolvePermutation(icaOutputs, lipScores) {
  // Assign frequency bins to sources based on highest lip correlation
  return assignFrequencyBins(icaOutputs, lipScores);
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests fixed-point arithmetic awareness, online adaptation, and practical trade-offs for beginner ICA workflows in constrained hardware.

## Key Concepts
- Fixed-point whitening and stability under quantization
- Online demixer updates and gradient projection
- Per-bin ICA vs joint diagonalization in nonstationary noise
- Envelope-based permutation tracking across frames

## Code Example
```javascript
function updateDemixer(W, x, step) {
  // simplified, placeholder fixed-point-like update
  const y = W.map(row => row.reduce((acc, w, i) => acc + w * x[i], 0));
  const grad = y.map(v => v);
  for (let r = 0; r < W.length; r++) {
    for (let c = 0; c < W[0].length; c++) {
      W[r][c] -= step * grad[r];
    }
  }
  return W;
}
```

